A||N||20||turbo86se||Progress!!!! ||||10||
Z||000000||turbo86se||11-04-2000||03:37 PM||||Alright!!  I just got off the phone with my mechanic, the V6 and auto tranny are mounted on the cradle! He said he'd like to get the set-up in the Fiero by the end of next week!! YEAH!!<P>Just to refresh everyone's memory, I'm converting my yellow 88 coupe with T-Tops to a V6. The V6 is from a 88 Formula, with 56K miles, in excellent condition. This conversion has taken a bit longer than I anticipated, but I know it will be worth the wait!!<P>Keep looking here for updates!! Thanks! <P>"Champagne breakfast for everyone"!!||||reg||10
Z||000001||2xsess||11-04-2000||04:20 PM||||LOL that my mechanic thing still gets me.<P>Anyways it sounds great, glad to here that someone is progressing!!! and if it turns out anything like your SE then It will be a knockout.<P>ohh Champagne breakfast sounds good too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 11-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||HAGS||11-04-2000||07:54 PM||||How much does an engine conversion cost?  Say a 2.5L V4 to 2.8L V6?||||reg||1
Z||000003||ArchMagi||11-04-2000||08:42 PM||||I assume you ment In-line4, they don't make V4 fieros.  Just thought id point that out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>~Archmagi||||reg||1
Z||000004||HAGS||11-04-2000||08:55 PM||||Yes, from my Iron Duke to the V6 that the GT's and SE's use.||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||11-05-2000||12:24 AM||||Jeff, if I get my coupe back on the road, I'm going to be driving it for a LONG time. This has been a T-Top Fieroless summer, and I miss it. Aside from driving my 86SE everyonce in a while, I've been Fieroless, sniff, sniff. <BR>It will take a while, the interior is trashed, but the coupe does look good, nothing like my 86SE!!<BR>If I get it on the road soon, I'll drive it down to Jacksonville for the next meeting. Time to put the turbo to sleep for a few months!!<P>HAGS, I really don't know how much this conversion would cost, my mechanic is a friend of mine, and we've worked out a trade, I just bought the engine, he does the install. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||11-11-2000||03:42 PM||||Yippee!! Time to get dirty!<BR>Today we removed the old spark plugs, Mike, my mechanic, did something to clean out the insides, and got the V6 turning effortlessly. <P>We removed the manifolds, cleaned the block, re-installed the manifolds with new Fel-Pro gaskets. Then we painted the tranny, frame, and a bunch of brackets. It looks real nice!!!<P>By now he should be changing the oil, installing the tranny filter, and putting in new tranny fluid! <P>Now I'm in search of some sensors, does anyone have an extra thermostat cap? $12 at the Fiero Store?<P>GETTING CLOSE!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000007||2xsess||11-11-2000||03:56 PM||||Can't wait to see it Joel!!!!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||4
Z||000008||beachbomb||11-12-2000||07:45 PM||||Glad to hear alls going well Joel!! Keep it up, can't wait to see it...Jim <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR>p.s. i'll luk when the pics arrive here, thanks again for that! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000009||turbo86se||11-15-2000||03:48 PM||||Thanks for the compliements guys, I appreciate it!!<P>Today we installed a new oil pressure sending unit, water temp sensor, 180 degree thermostat, and got the correct bolts to bolt it to the frame securely.<P>It looks like it may be going into the car on Friday!!  I hope the weather's nice!!||||reg||14
Z||000010||2xsess||11-15-2000||04:00 PM||||Joel, I hope it's warmer there than it has been here. lol.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||turbo86se||01-11-2001||05:22 PM||||Today we got the exhaust installed. Welded on a new "test pipe" where the cat used to be. Looks real good, nice and smooth. Mike also re-drilled a new fitting for something above the oil filter. It's basically ready to go in. I do need a couple things:<BR>*Kickdown cable for auto V6, 1988<BR>*Starter for V6<BR>Anyone have any extra laying around? LMK!<P>Hopefully tomorrow we'll get it in the car, on four wheels, and be able to get it to my mechanic's house for the wiring and fuel pump!<BR> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||10
Z||000012||turbo86se||01-25-2001||06:06 PM||||Today we pushed, pulled, grunted and cussed! The whole engine/cradle assembly is under the car! Now I can look down into the engine bay and see a sweet Fiero V6 engine! Now we're ready to install the Formula struts, and lower the car onto the assembly! I brought back my original 13" wheels from my old '85 coupe in MD to put on until I get it aligned. <P>My brother-in-law called me today, and I'm an uncle!!!!!!  YIPPEEE!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>More champagne breakfast for everyone!!||||reg||10
Z||000013||zeusrekning||01-25-2001||06:51 PM||||ok joel afte you get the 88 finished, you'll deliver it when? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||2xsess||01-25-2001||08:11 PM||||Wow, what a week for you!! <P>Can't wait for the "Fired it up today" post  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">   <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||turbo86se||03-03-2001||12:38 AM||||It's IN!!<P>The V6 engine assembly is mounted and bolted up into my 88 coupe! I've been overly patient and persistant, and now hopefully the car is on four wheels for the first time in nearly a year. I can't wait to drive my coupe! Tops off, warm weather, nice sun-burn...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>We did run into a problem, we tried installing the temporary 13" wheels, and the calipers were hitting the inside of the wheels. Tried it with the stock 14" wheels, same thing. I don't know if he had any luck with the Formula wheels. Why would that be? We're almost there. Once I get my coupe back I won't drive my '00 Altima for three months!!! <P>YEAH!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||DRH||03-03-2001||12:50 AM||||I have heard 13" won't fit 88s. The 14" wheels should fit though. My winter rims on my 88 Formula are 14" turbo fin (or whatever they're called) off an 86 SE. They fit fine.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||turbo86se||03-11-2001||11:56 AM||||The other day we got my beautiful Fiero off the jackstands. Now it's on it's own four wheels. It looks sooo good! We pushed if from the backyard to the driveway. Hopefully today we'll get it towed to my mechanic's house, along with a nice red '88 coupe he bought for next to nothing. <P>Can't wait to fire it up!||||reg||10
Z||000018||Homicidal||03-11-2001||02:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by HAGS:<BR><B>How much does an engine conversion cost?  Say a 2.5L V4 to 2.8L V6?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I second that question, anybody?||||reg||1
Z||000019||JBGehling||03-11-2001||03:12 PM||||I wouldn't imagine much more than  $1,000.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||tgowens||03-11-2001||05:20 PM||||a conversion from a 2.5 to a 2.8 will cost quite a bit more than $1,000 counting the engine and the labor to do the install........there is quite a bit of difference between the two in terms of cooling hoses, wiring, etc.........we have done several here in the shop and it takes a considerable amount of time......||||reg||1
